t in play.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Neal Dunn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 2nd District is a Republican-leaning open seat after Neal Dunn's retirement, with a partisan lean of about eight points toward the GOP. Austin Rogers secured the Republican nomination in August and enters the general election with a large financial edge, having raised roughly $1 million and drawn about $1.4 million in outside support. Democrat Amanda Green has run an active campaign and hit fundraising milestones, but she has raised far less and reported limited cash on hand.\n\nNo reliable public general-election polling exists; the few available surveys are partisan and hypothetical. Expert raters overwhelmingly place the seat in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-ten chance. The race has drawn local attention, including an agreed debate and questions about Rogers' family residence, but nothing yet suggests a fundamental shift. The forecast expects Republicans to hold the seat comfortably, with Green needing an unusually favorable late break to compete.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1162, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1045, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0789, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0848, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1006, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0806, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0753, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0679, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0853, "margin": -9.5}]}